---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = 'https://www.dg-sdk.com';
const url = base + '/blog/compressed-air-purity-surface-cleaning';
const title = 'Compressed Air for Surface Cleaning: Particles, Water and Oil';
const seoTitle = 'Compressed Air Purity for Surface Cleaning';
const description = 'Review compressed-air purity for a proposed surface-cleaning process: particle, water and oil requirements, pressure dew point and the sampling location.';
---

<Layout title={seoTitle + ' | Shidike'} description={description} canonical={url}
  image="/assets/img/blog/compressed-air-purity-v1.jpg">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: base },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: base + '/blog' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: title, item: url }
    ]
  })} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'BlogPosting', headline: title, description,
    image: base + '/assets/img/blog/compressed-air-purity-v1.jpg',
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Shidike', url: base },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Shidike', legalName: 'Dongguan Shidike Intelligent Equipment Co., Ltd.', url: base },
    datePublished: '2026-11-12', dateModified: '2026-11-12', mainEntityOfPage: url
  })} />

  <article class="post">
    <header class="post-head">
      <div class="container post-col">
        <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/blog">Blog</a><span>/</span>Compressed Air Purity</div>
        <div class="post-tags"><span class="blog-tag">Surface Cleaning</span><span class="blog-tag">Compressed Air</span><span class="blog-tag">Application Planning</span></div>
        <h1>{title}</h1>
        <p class="post-lead">If a proposed surface-cleaning process uses compressed air at the material, ask what air quality is required and where it will be checked. A useful brief names the contaminant groups and connects each requirement to an identified location.</p>
        <div class="post-info"><span>November 12, 2026</span><span>Shidike Technical Team</span><span>3 min read</span></div>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="container post-col post-body">
      <picture class="post-figure">
        <source media="(max-width: 600px)" srcset="/assets/img/blog/compressed-air-purity-v1-mobile.webp" type="image/webp" width="800" height="1400" />
        <source media="(max-width: 600px)" srcset="/assets/img/blog/compressed-air-purity-v1-mobile.jpg" type="image/jpeg" width="800" height="1400" />
        <source srcset="/assets/img/blog/compressed-air-purity-v1.webp" type="image/webp" />
        <img src="/assets/img/blog/compressed-air-purity-v1.jpg" alt="Concept diagram naming particles, water and oil above a supply path with sampling location A upstream and B at the point of use." width="1600" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </picture>
      <p><em>Original documentation diagram. A and B identify different locations; neither has a measured result. No purity class or equipment configuration is specified.</em></p>

      <section id="three-contaminant-groups">
        <h2>Read particles, water and oil separately</h2>
        <p>The official <a href="https://www.iso.org/standard/46418.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ISO 8573-1:2010 abstract</a> describes compressed-air purity classes for particles, water and oil. It also identifies gaseous and microbiological contaminants, so the three groups are not a claim that every possible contaminant has been assessed.</p>
        <p>The <a href="https://www.cagi.org/assets/documents/pdfs/publications/cagi-compressed-air-purity-guide.pdf?updated=1755803863" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CAGI Compressed Air Purity Guide, page 3</a>, explains the designation order: particles, then water, then oil. Keep those labels beside the class entries. A lone class number leaves the category unclear.</p>
        <p>This article does not select a class for film, PCB or another material. The proposed equipment and application need their own documented requirements; naming the standard does not supply those missing choices.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="pressure-dew-point">
        <h2>Keep the pressure basis with a dew-point value</h2>
        <p>A water-related report may include a pressure dew point. The <a href="https://www.cagi.org/resource-library.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CAGI glossary</a> defines this as the temperature at which water begins to condense from air at a given pressure. The pressure is part of the meaning of the value.</p>
        <p>For example, an unlabeled temperature in a proposal needs clarification: is it a pressure dew point, and at what pressure? Retain the original quantity name, unit and pressure basis in the review. Do not silently treat an atmospheric dew point and a pressure dew point as interchangeable. No dryer setting or target temperature is prescribed here.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sampling-location">
        <h2>Match the report location to the question</h2>
        <p><a href="https://www.cagi.org/assets/documents/pdfs/publications/cagi-compressed-air-purity-guide.pdf?updated=1755803863" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CAGI's purity guide, page 16</a>, notes that the distribution network can add contamination between the compressor room and the point of use. An upstream report therefore should not be relabeled as a result at the cleaning connection.</p>
        <p>Consider an invented proposal: its air-quality report identifies A, while the requirement names B. Mark that mismatch and request evidence addressing B. This does not prove that B is contaminated or that the proposal fails; it identifies a question the supplied report has not answered.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="air-quality-brief">
        <h2>Use a blank brief before comparing proposals</h2>
        <p>The following is an original project worksheet, not an ISO test form. Complete it with the equipment supplier and the person responsible for the material process. Keep unknown entries open instead of assigning a generic class.</p>
        <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Blank compressed-air requirement and evidence worksheet">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Project requirement</th><th scope="col">Evidence supplied</th><th scope="col">Open question</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row">Particles</th><td>Class / criterion: ___</td><td>Report / result: ___</td><td>___</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Water</th><td>Class / criterion: ___</td><td>Quantity / unit / pressure basis: ___</td><td>___</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Oil</th><td>Class / criterion: ___</td><td>Report / result: ___</td><td>___</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Location</th><td>Named connection: ___</td><td>Sampling point / date: ___</td><td>___</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>Attach the document revision, report identifier and agreed test method rather than copying isolated figures into a quotation comparison. Identify who will resolve each open question and retain the original report with the decision.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="air-and-cleaning-results">
        <h2>Evaluate the material result separately</h2>
        <p>An air-purity result describes the supplied air. It is not a particle-removal percentage or proof that the cleaned surface meets its acceptance criterion. Keep the air specification and the material-trial result as separate evidence in the equipment review.</p>
        <p>For the different question of supply pressure and particle-removal evidence, see <a href="/blog/air-jet-particle-removal-pressure">reviewing air-jet cleaning proposals</a>. For the broader choice between contact and air/extraction methods, see <a href="/guides/what-is-web-cleaning">our web-cleaning guide</a>.</p>
      </section>
      <div class="post-cta">
        <h2>Define the process before specifying its utilities</h2>
        <p>Share the material, contamination and proposed cleaning method with Shidike. Confirm the selected machine's utility requirements from its current documentation; this generic brief does not assign an air-purity class to a Shidike model.</p>
        <p><a class="send-cta" href="/products/cleaning-machine">Explore Cleaning Machines &rarr;</a><a class="send-alt" href="/contact?type=selection&amp;product=Surface%20Cleaning%20Air%20Quality%20Review">Discuss your cleaning application &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
  <style>
    .post-col { max-width: 780px; }
    .post-head { background: #f7f8fa; padding: 48px 0 34px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
    .post-head .breadcrumb { font-size: 13px; color: #7d8d97; margin-bottom: 18px; }
    .post-head .breadcrumb a { color: var(--brand-deep); text-decoration: none; }
    .post-head .breadcrumb span { margin: 0 8px; }
    .post-tags { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; margin-bottom: 14px; }
    .blog-tag {
      font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase;
      background: #eef4f8; color: #4a6373; padding: 4px 9px; border-radius: 999px;
    }
    .post-head h1 {
      font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.4vw, 2.5rem); line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: -.02em; color: var(--navy); margin: 0 0 14px;
    }
    .post-lead { font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #46545f; margin: 0 0 18px; }
    .post-info { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px; font-size: 12.5px; color: #8a99a4; }

    .post-body { padding: 34px 0 70px; }
    .post-figure { display: block; margin: 0 0 30px; }
    .post-figure img {
      display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 8px;
    }
    .post-body h2 {
      font-size: 1.42rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.01em; color: var(--navy);
      margin: 34px 0 12px;
    }
    .post-body p { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.78; color: #3d4a54; margin: 0 0 15px; }
    .post-body a { color: var(--brand-deep); }
    .post-body h3 {
      font-size: 1.12rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); margin: 26px 0 10px;
    }
    .post-body ul, .post-body ol { margin: 0 0 15px; padding-left: 22px; }
    .post-body li { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.78; color: #3d4a54; margin: 0 0 7px; }
    .post-body blockquote, .post-body .blog-quote {
      margin: 0 0 18px; padding: 13px 16px; background: #f2f6f9;
      border-left: 3px solid var(--brand-deep); border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
    }
    .post-body .blog-quote p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .post-body .step-block { margin: 0 0 22px; }
    .post-body .step-num {
      display: inline-block; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .06em;
      text-transform: uppercase; background: var(--navy); color: #fff;
      padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 999px; margin-bottom: 8px;
    }
    .formula {
      font-size: 1.2rem !important; font-weight: 700; text-align: center; color: var(--navy) !important;
      background: #f2f6f9; border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 8px; padding: 14px;
    }

    .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin: 0 0 20px; }
    .post-body table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 14.5px; }
    .post-body th, .post-body td {
      text-align: left; padding: 10px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline); vertical-align: top;
    }
    .post-body thead th { background: #f2f6f9; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); }
    .post-body tbody th { width: 22%; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); background: #fafbfc; }

    .faq-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; margin: 6px 0 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
    .faq-item { padding: 15px 4px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline); }
    .faq-item summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); font-size: 15.5px; }
    .faq-item p { margin: 10px 0 0; }

    .post-cta {
      margin-top: 40px; padding: 26px 26px 22px; background: #f7f8fa;
      border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 10px;
    }
    .post-cta h2 { margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.25rem; }
    .send-cta, .send-alt { display: inline-block; font-weight: 700; margin-right: 22px; }
    @media (max-width: 767px) {
      .post-body { padding-left: 16px; padding-right: 16px; }
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
